  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Whenever you successfully distract a creature with either a Bluff check to create a diversion or an Intimidate check to pose a menace (new skill use), the creature remains distracted until the end of your next turn and the creature must succeed at a Will saving throw or be fascinated by either you or the diversion while distracted. You can prolong the duration of the fascinated condition by 1 round as a standard action, up to a maximum of 1 round per rank you possess in the associated skill.</p>\n<p>In addition to the usual ways to end it, the fascinated condition ends if any creature the fascinated creature can perceive takes a hostile action or is damaged.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/bluster#toc9\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
